# =============================================================================
# File:    Reservations.http
# Author:  Thisuri
# Created: 2026-09-27
# Purpose: Manual test script for the M3 Reservation API
#          (docs/api-contract.md §4). Run with the VS Code "REST Client"
#          extension (humao.rest-client): click "Send Request" above each one.
#          Every request states the result it must produce (EXPECT ...).
#
# Needs a fresh seed (docs/seed/seed-database.js) — slot times are relative
# to when the seed ran. Run A first; later sections reuse its tokens and the
# id captured from B1. The automated edge cases (exactly 7 days, concurrent
# last space, double cancel) are in SmartSolar.Api.Tests/ReservationFlowTests.
# Section F cancels what this script created, so it can be re-run.
# =============================================================================

@base = http://localhost:5199/api
@password = Test@1234

@bo = {{loginBO.response.body.$.token}}
@op = {{loginOP.response.body.$.token}}
@p1 = {{loginP1.response.body.$.token}}

# Seed data
@otherNic = 200012345672
@slot26h = 670000000000000000000002
@slot50h = 670000000000000000000003
@slot8h = 670000000000000000000001
@slotCap1 = 670000000000000000000019
@slot200h = 670000000000000000000020
@slotInactiveNode = 670000000000000000000017

@resId = {{create.response.body.$.id}}
@res8h = {{create8h.response.body.$.id}}


# =============================================================================
# A. Logins
# =============================================================================

### A1 — EXPECT 200
# @name loginBO
POST {{base}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "username": "backoffice.admin", "password": "{{password}}" }

### A2 — EXPECT 200
# @name loginOP
POST {{base}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "username": "operator.colombo", "password": "{{password}}" }

### A3 — EXPECT 200
# @name loginP1
POST {{base}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "username": "nimal.perera", "password": "{{password}}" }


# =============================================================================
# B. Create (R1, duplicate, capacity)
# =============================================================================

### B1 Prosumer books a slot 26 h out — EXPECT 201, status Pending, Location header.
# The body prosumerNIC is IGNORED for a prosumer: prosumerNIC in the response is the token's.
# @name create
POST {{base}}/reservations
Authorization: Bearer {{p1}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "slotId": "{{slot26h}}", "energyKWh": 10, "prosumerNIC": "{{otherNic}}" }

### B2 Same slot again — EXPECT 409 RESERVATION_DUPLICATE
POST {{base}}/reservations
Authorization: Bearer {{p1}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "slotId": "{{slot26h}}", "energyKWh": 5 }

### B3 Slot 200 h (8+ days) out — EXPECT 422 RESERVATION_OUTSIDE_WINDOW
POST {{base}}/reservations
Authorization: Bearer {{p1}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "slotId": "{{slot200h}}", "energyKWh": 5 }

### B4 Slot on the Inactive node — EXPECT 409 RESERVATION_NODE_INACTIVE
POST {{base}}/reservations
Authorization: Bearer {{p1}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "slotId": "{{slotInactiveNode}}", "energyKWh": 5 }

### B5 Energy above the slot's 30 kWh — EXPECT 400 RESERVATION_INVALID_ENERGY
POST {{base}}/reservations
Authorization: Bearer {{p1}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "slotId": "{{slot50h}}", "energyKWh": 31 }

### B6 Backoffice books the capacity-1 slot for another prosumer — EXPECT 201 (slot flips to Full)
POST {{base}}/reservations
Authorization: Bearer {{bo}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "slotId": "{{slotCap1}}", "energyKWh": 5, "prosumerNIC": "{{otherNic}}" }

### B7 Prosumer tries the now-full slot — EXPECT 409 RESERVATION_SLOT_FULL
POST {{base}}/reservations
Authorization: Bearer {{p1}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "slotId": "{{slotCap1}}", "energyKWh": 5 }

### B8 Backoffice without prosumerNIC — EXPECT 400 USER_NIC_INVALID
POST {{base}}/reservations
Authorization: Bearer {{bo}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "slotId": "{{slot50h}}", "energyKWh": 5 }

### B9 Grid Operator cannot create — EXPECT 403 AUTH_FORBIDDEN_ROLE
POST {{base}}/reservations
Authorization: Bearer {{op}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "slotId": "{{slot50h}}", "energyKWh": 5 }

### B10 Book the slot starting in 8 h (allowed by R1) — EXPECT 201. Used by D2.
# @name create8h
POST {{base}}/reservations
Authorization: Bearer {{p1}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "slotId": "{{slot8h}}", "energyKWh": 5 }


# =============================================================================
# C. Reads
# =============================================================================

### C1 Own detail — EXPECT 200
GET {{base}}/reservations/{{resId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{p1}}

### C2 Mine, Pending only — EXPECT 200 array (no nic parameter exists)
GET {{base}}/reservations/mine?status=Pending
Authorization: Bearer {{p1}}

### C3 Staff search — EXPECT 200 {items, page, pageSize, totalCount, totalPages}
GET {{base}}/reservations?status=Pending&page=1&pageSize=5
Authorization: Bearer {{op}}

### C4 Staff search by NIC (lower-case v/x is normalised) — EXPECT 200
GET {{base}}/reservations?nic={{otherNic}}
Authorization: Bearer {{bo}}

### C5 Prosumer on the staff search — EXPECT 403 AUTH_FORBIDDEN_ROLE
GET {{base}}/reservations
Authorization: Bearer {{p1}}

### C6 Unknown status filter — EXPECT 400 RESERVATION_INVALID_STATUS_FILTER
GET {{base}}/reservations?status=Booked
Authorization: Bearer {{op}}

### C7 Malformed id — EXPECT 404 RESERVATION_NOT_FOUND
GET {{base}}/reservations/not-an-id
Authorization: Bearer {{p1}}


# =============================================================================
# D. Update (R2 on current, R1 + capacity on new)
# =============================================================================

### D1 Move B1 to the 50 h slot — EXPECT 200, slotId/slotStart changed
PUT {{base}}/reservations/{{resId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{p1}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "slotId": "{{slot50h}}", "energyKWh": 12 }

### D2 Update the 8 h booking — EXPECT 409 RESERVATION_NOTICE_PERIOD ("starts in 7 hour(s) ...")
PUT {{base}}/reservations/{{res8h}}
Authorization: Bearer {{p1}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "slotId": "{{slot50h}}", "energyKWh": 5 }

### D3 Move B1 to the full slot — EXPECT 409 RESERVATION_SLOT_FULL, booking unchanged (check C1)
PUT {{base}}/reservations/{{resId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{p1}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "slotId": "{{slotCap1}}", "energyKWh": 5 }


# =============================================================================
# E. Approve / reject (GridOperator only)
# =============================================================================

### E1 Prosumer approves — EXPECT 403 AUTH_FORBIDDEN_ROLE
PATCH {{base}}/reservations/{{resId}}/approve
Authorization: Bearer {{p1}}

### E2 Backoffice approves — EXPECT 403 AUTH_FORBIDDEN_ROLE
PATCH {{base}}/reservations/{{resId}}/approve
Authorization: Bearer {{bo}}

### E3 Operator approves — EXPECT 200, status Approved, approvedBy + approvedAt set
PATCH {{base}}/reservations/{{resId}}/approve
Authorization: Bearer {{op}}

### E4 Approve again — EXPECT 409 RESERVATION_INVALID_STATE
PATCH {{base}}/reservations/{{resId}}/approve
Authorization: Bearer {{op}}

### E5 Reject an Approved booking — EXPECT 409 RESERVATION_INVALID_STATE
PATCH {{base}}/reservations/{{resId}}/reject
Authorization: Bearer {{op}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "reason": "Grid maintenance" }

### E6 Reject without a reason — EXPECT 400 (validation, errors.Reason)
PATCH {{base}}/reservations/{{res8h}}/reject
Authorization: Bearer {{op}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ }


# =============================================================================
# F. Cancel (R2) — also cleans up
# =============================================================================

### F1 Cancel the 8 h booking — EXPECT 409 RESERVATION_NOTICE_PERIOD
PATCH {{base}}/reservations/{{res8h}}/cancel
Authorization: Bearer {{p1}}

### F2 Android-style cancel (POST + override) of B1 — EXPECT 200, status Cancelled, cancelledAt set
POST {{base}}/reservations/{{resId}}/cancel
Authorization: Bearer {{p1}}
X-HTTP-Method-Override: PATCH

### F3 Cancel B1 again — EXPECT 409 RESERVATION_INVALID_STATE (capacity NOT released twice)
PATCH {{base}}/reservations/{{resId}}/cancel
Authorization: Bearer {{p1}}

### F4 Operator rejects the 8 h booking (reject has no 12 h rule) — EXPECT 200, capacity released
PATCH {{base}}/reservations/{{res8h}}/reject
Authorization: Bearer {{op}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "reason": "Test clean-up" }

# B6 (the capacity-1 slot for {{otherNic}}) is left in place: it is what makes
# B7 and D3 demonstrate SLOT_FULL. Cancel it from the staff search (C4) with
# Backoffice if you want the slot back to Open.
